# Generated UniFFI integration artifacts (reproduce with scripts/build-jni.sh).
# The Rust cdylib .so (per-ABI, ~20MB each) and the uniffi-bindgen Kotlin
# bindings are build outputs, not source — mirrors clients/ios's Generated/.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately. A trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY only, so
# when these paths are SYMLINKS — which is how every git worktree gets them,
# pointed at the primary checkout so a worktree need not rebuild 20MB per ABI —
# the rule missed them, they surfaced as untracked, and a `git add clients/`
# committed five absolute symlinks whose targets were their own checked-out
# paths. Checking that out replaced the real build inputs with self-referential
# links and made every tree walk fail with ELOOP.
app/src/main/jniLibs
app/src/direct/jniLibs
app/src/play/jniLibs
app/src/main/java/com/lingxi/code/bindings
app/libs

.gradle/
build/
app/build/
local.properties
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
.kotlin/
captures/
*.apk

# Device-acceptance secret: the write-scoped PAT for the Git auth tests is
# written here locally and read by the test runner — never committed.
.gittoken
app/libs/*.aar
